@startuml
title Teamparature - Use Case Diagram
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
actor Guest
actor "Registered user" as User
actor "Workspace member" as Member
actor "Workspace owner" as Owner
actor "Email service" as Email
Member --|> User
Owner --|> Member
rectangle Teamparature {
usecase "Register / log in" as Auth
usecase "Log out" as Logout
usecase "Create workspace" as Create
usecase "Join by code / accept invitation" as Join
usecase "View / switch workspaces" as Switch
usecase "Submit daily mood check-in" as Check
usecase "View own mood history" as History
usecase "View team dashboard and analytics" as Analytics
usecase "View, remove and restore members" as Manage
usecase "Change member roles" as Roles
usecase "Send / resend invitations" as Invite
usecase "Send invitation email" as Send
usecase "View / cancel invitations" as Cancel
usecase "View activity history" as Activity
usecase "Update workspace settings" as Settings
usecase "Delete workspace" as Delete
}
Guest -- Auth
User -- Logout
User -- Create
User -- Join
User -- Switch
Member -- Check
Member -- History
Owner -- Analytics
Owner -- Manage
Owner -- Roles
Owner -- Invite
Owner -- Cancel
Owner -- Activity
Owner -- Settings
Owner -- Delete
Invite ..> Send : <<include>>
Email -- Send
note bottom of Check
Mood, intensity and optional note.
One check-in per workspace day.
end note
note bottom of Roles
Cannot remove or demote the last owner.
end note
@enduml
